	meta={['Formal + casual', 'Polite -करा ending', 'Unit 02']}
	faq={[
		{
			question: 'What is the Marathi word for please?',
			answer: 'The formal word is कृपया (kṛpayā), but in daily speech the polite imperative ending -करा does the work: बस करा (please sit), द्या करा (please give), या करा (please come).'
		},
		{
			question: 'Is "please" always कृपया in Marathi?',
			answer: 'No. कृपया is formal (signs, letters). In conversation, use the verb + करा pattern: पाणी द्या करा (water give-please), माफ करा (excuse me/forgive-please).'
		},
		{
			question: 'How do you say "yes, please" in Marathi?',
			answer: 'हो, कृपया (ho, kṛpayā) — literally "yes, please."'
