>

<h1>{title}</h1>

<p class="lead">The go-to word for <strong>please</strong> in Marathi is <strong>कृपया</strong> (kṛpayā) — but real politeness lives in the verb ending <strong>-करा</strong> (imperative polite) and the softener <strong>-न</strong> particles. This guide covers the word, the grammar, and the phrases you'll actually hear.</p>

<h2>Quick Answer</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Marathi</th><th>Transliteration</th><th>Context</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>कृपया</td><td>kṛpayā</td><td>Formal please (signs, writing)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>कृपया करा</td><td>kṛpayā karā</td><td>Please do (polite request)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>कृपया बस/ठेवा</td><td>kṛpayā bas/ṭhevā</td><td>Please sit / please keep</td></tr>
    <tr><td>हो, कृपया</td><td>ho, kṛpayā</td><td>Yes, please</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Grammar: The Polite Imperative -करा</h2>
<p>Marathi makes requests polite by adding <strong>-करा</strong> to the verb stem (not कृपया alone):</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>बस</strong> (sit) → <strong>बस करा</strong> (please sit)</li>
  <li><strong>आ</strong> (come) → <strong>या करा</strong> (please come — irregular stem)</li>
  <li><strong>दे</strong> (give) → <strong>द्या करा</strong> (please give)</li>
  <li><strong>सांग</strong> (tell) → <strong>सांगा करा</strong> (please tell)</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip-box"><strong>Tip:</strong> कृपया is formal (signs, letters). In speech, the <strong>-करा</strong> ending does the heavy lifting. Say <em>पाणी द्या करा</em> (water give-please) more often than <em>कृपया पाणी द्या</em>.</div>

<h2>Real-Life Patterns</h2>
<table class="vocab-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Marathi</th><th>Literal</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Ordering chai</td><td>एक चहा द्या करा</td><td>One tea give-please</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Asking for water</td><td>पाणी द्या करा</td><td>Water give-please</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Requesting directions</td><td>मला रस्ता सांगा करा</td><td>To-me route tell-please</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Excuse me / pardon</td><td>माफ करा</td><td>Forgive-please</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Yes, please</td><td>हो, कृपया</td><td>Yes, please</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>❌ कृपया बस</strong> → <strong>✅ बस करा</strong> (कृपया alone sounds like a sign)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ कृपया आ</strong> → <strong>✅ या करा</strong> (come has irregular stem या)</li>
  <li><strong>❌ प्लिज़</strong> → Don't use English "please" — use कृपया or -करा</li>
</ul>

<h2>Mini Practice</h2>
<ol>
  <li>How do you say "Please give water"? → <em>पाणी द्या करा</em></li>
  <li>How do you say "Please sit"? → <em>बस करा</em></li>
  <li>How do you say "Excuse me"? → <em>माफ करा</em></li>
</ol>

